==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|stellen}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*stallijaną}}. More at {{l|en|stell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈʃtɛln̩]|[ˈʃtɛlən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-stellen.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-stellen.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|stellt|stellte|gestellt}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[pose]] (a question, a riddle)
#: ''Kann ich dir eine Frage stellen?''
#:: Can I pose a question to you?
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[position]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[put]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[catch]]
#: ''Die [[Polizei]] stellte den Dieb.''
#:: The police caught the thief.
# {{lb|de|figurative|colloquial}} to [[corner]]
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[surrender]]
#: ''Der [[Dieb]] '''stellte sich''' der Polizei.''
#:: The thief surrendered to the police.
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[set]], [[adjust]] {{qualifier|a clock}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[place]] oneself, [[get]]
# {{lb|de|reflexive|with gerund or adjective}} to [[feign]], to [[pretend]] to

